{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-64656" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by arc length $s.$ Find the curvature at the point where $s=\\pi $ if the unit tangent vector of the curve is given by\n\n$$\nT(s)=\\frac{1}{2}⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}),\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}),\\,\\sqrt{3}⟩.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-64656" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since we are given that the curve $r(s)$ and its unit tangent vector $T(s)$ are parametrized by the arc length $s$, we will use the following formula for the curvature: \n\n$$\nκ(s)=‖{T}^{′}(s)‖\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $T(s)$ with respect to $s$ and evaluate it at $s=\\pi $:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(s) & =\\frac{1}{2}⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\sqrt{3})⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}⟨-(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}),\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})\\cdot \\frac{1}{2},\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}),\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}),\\,0⟩ \\\\ {T}^{′}(\\pi ) & =\\text{ }\\frac{1}{4}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}),\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}),\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}⟨1,\\,0,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain the curvature:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(\\pi ) & =‖{T}^{′}(\\pi )‖=\\frac{1}{4}\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{0}^{2}}=\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-64656" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5e94acaae172a715aeef078197f31f678d672b149d01e9b726683c3b9ee790e8"} {"question" "q-64656" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-64656" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2\\sqrt{3}"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-64656" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-83661" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by arc length $s.$ Find the curvature at the point where $s=\\pi $ if the unit tangent vector of the curve is given by\n\n$$\nT(s)=⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{3}),\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})⟩.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-83661" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since we are given that the curve $r(s)$ and its unit tangent vector $T(s)$ are parametrized by the arc length $s$, we will use the following formula for the curvature: \n\n$$\nκ(s)=‖{T}^{′}(s)‖\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $T(s)$ with respect to $s$ and evaluate it at $s=\\pi :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{3}))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})\\cdot \\frac{1}{3},\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{3}),\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})⟩ \\\\ {T}^{′}(\\pi ) & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}),\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},\\,-\\frac{1}{2}⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}⟨\\sqrt{3},\\,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain the curvature:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(\\pi ) & =‖{T}^{′}(\\pi )‖ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot \\sqrt{(\\sqrt{3})^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot \\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-83661" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5e94acaae172a715aeef078197f31f678d672b149d01e9b726683c3b9ee790e8"} {"question" "q-83661" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-83661" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{6}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-83661" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-83660" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by arc length $s.$ Find the curvature at the point where $s=\\frac{1}{4}$ if the unit tangent vector of the curve is given by\n\n \n\n$$\nT(s)=-\\sqrt{1-2s}\\,i+\\sqrt{2s}\\,j.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-83660" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since we are given that the curve $r(s)$ and its unit tangent vector $T(s)$ are parametrized by the arc length $s$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(s)=‖{T}^{′}(s)‖\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $T(s)$ with respect to $s$ and evaluate it at $s=\\frac{1}{4}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\sqrt{1-2s})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\sqrt{2s})\\,j \\\\  & =-\\frac{-2}{2\\sqrt{1-2s}}\\,i+\\frac{2}{2\\sqrt{2s}}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-2s}}\\,i+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2s}}\\,j \\\\ {T}^{′}(\\frac{1}{4}) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-2(\\frac{1}{4})}}\\,i+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2(\\frac{1}{4})}}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{2}}}\\,i+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{2}}}\\,j \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\,i+\\sqrt{2}\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we obtain the curvature:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(\\frac{1}{4}) & =‖{T}^{′}(\\frac{1}{4})‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(\\sqrt{2})}^{2}+{(\\sqrt{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-83660" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5e94acaae172a715aeef078197f31f678d672b149d01e9b726683c3b9ee790e8"} {"question" "q-83660" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-83660" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-83660" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-34278" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by arc length $s.$ Find the curvature at the point where $s=5\\pi $, if the unit tangent vector of the curve is given by\n\n \n\n$$\nT(s)=\\frac{4}{5}\\,i-\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3s}{5})\\,j+\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3s}{5})\\,k.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-34278" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since we are given that the curve $r(s)$ and its unit tangent vector $T(s)$ are parametrized by the arc length $s$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(s)=‖{T}^{′}(s)‖\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $T(s)$ with respect to $s$ and evaluate it at $s=5\\pi $: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{4}{5})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3s}{5}))\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3s}{5}))\\,k \\\\  & =(0)\\,i-\\frac{9}{25}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3s}{5})\\,j-\\frac{9}{25}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3s}{5})\\,k \\\\ {T}^{′}(5\\pi ) & =-\\frac{9}{25}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\cdot (5\\pi )}{5})\\,j-\\frac{9}{25}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\cdot (5\\pi )}{5})\\,k \\\\  & =-\\frac{9}{25}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\pi )\\,j-\\frac{9}{25}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\pi )\\,k \\\\  & =-\\frac{9}{25}\\cdot (-1)\\,j-\\frac{9}{25}\\cdot (0)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{25}\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we obtain the curvature:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(5\\pi ) & =‖{T}^{′}(5\\pi )‖ \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{25}\\sqrt{{(0)}^{2}+{(1)}^{2}+{(0)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{25}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-34278" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5e94acaae172a715aeef078197f31f678d672b149d01e9b726683c3b9ee790e8"} {"question" "q-34278" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-34278" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{15}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{8}{19}"] ["math" "\\frac{9}{25}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-34278" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{9}{25}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-80607" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by arc length $s.$ Find the curvature at the point where $s=1$ if the unit tangent vector of the curve is given by\n\n$$\nT(s)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{s}^{2}}}⟨1,s⟩.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-80607" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since we are given that the curve $r(s)$ and its unit tangent vector $T(s)$ are parametrized by the arc length $s$, we will use the following formula for the curvature: \n\n$$\nκ(s)=‖{T}^{′}(s)‖\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $T(s)$ with respect to $s$ and evaluate it at $s=1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{s}^{2}}}⟨1,s⟩) \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{s}^{2}}}),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{s}{\\sqrt{1+{s}^{2}}})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{s}{(1+{s}^{2})^{3/2}},\\,\\frac{1}{(1+{s}^{2})^{3/2}}⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(1+{s}^{2})^{3/2}}⟨-s,1⟩ \\\\ {T}^{′}(1) & =\\frac{1}{(1+{1}^{2})^{3/2}}⟨-1,1⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}}⟨-1,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we obtain the curvature:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(1) & =‖{T}^{′}(1)‖ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}}‖⟨-1,1⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}}\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-80607" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5e94acaae172a715aeef078197f31f678d672b149d01e9b726683c3b9ee790e8"} {"question" "q-80607" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-80607" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-80607" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-131938" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by its arc length $s$, where\n\n$$\nr(s)=\\frac{1}{3}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡3s,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡3s⟩,\\,0\\le s\\le \\frac{2\\pi }{3}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-131938" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $T(s)$ denote the unit tangent to the given curve as a function of the arc length $s.$ Since we are given the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by the arc length $s$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(s)=‖{T}^{′}(s)‖=‖{r}^{″}(s)‖\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(s)$ and ${r}^{″}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(s) & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡3s),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡3s)⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡3s,\\,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡3s⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡3s,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡3s⟩ \\\\ {r}^{″}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡3s),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡3s)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡3s,\\,-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡3s⟩ \\\\  & =-3⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡3s,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡3s⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(s) & =‖{r}^{″}(s)‖ \\\\  & =|-3|\\cdot \\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡3s+{sin}^{2}⁡3s} \\\\  & =3\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-131938" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5e94acaae172a715aeef078197f31f678d672b149d01e9b726683c3b9ee790e8"} {"question" "q-131938" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-131938" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "9"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{9}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-131938" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-131931" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by its arc length $s$, where\n\n$$\nr(s)=⟨\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}),\\,\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}),\\frac{\\sqrt{5}s}{3}⟩,\\,0\\le s\\le 4\\pi .\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-131931" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $T(s)$ denote the unit tangent to the given curve as a function of the arc length $s.$ Since we are given the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by the arc length $s$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(s)=‖{T}^{′}(s)‖=‖{r}^{″}(s)‖\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(s)$ and ${r}^{″}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{\\sqrt{5}s}{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}),\\,\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}),\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}⟩ \\\\ {r}^{″}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}),\\,-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}),\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}),\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}),\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(s) & =‖{r}^{″}(s)‖ \\\\  & =|-\\frac{1}{3}|\\cdot \\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})+{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-131931" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5e94acaae172a715aeef078197f31f678d672b149d01e9b726683c3b9ee790e8"} {"question" "q-131931" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-131931" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-131931" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-80523" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by its arc length $s$, where\n\n$$\nr(s)=⟨5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{5}),\\,5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})⟩,\\,0\\le s<10\\pi .\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-80523" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $T(s)$ denote the unit tangent to the given curve as a function of the arc length $s.$ Since we are given the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by the arc length $s$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(s)=‖{T}^{′}(s)‖=‖{r}^{″}(s)‖\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(s)$ and ${r}^{″}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{5}))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})\\cdot \\frac{1}{5},\\,5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{5}),\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})⟩ \\\\ {r}^{″}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{5}))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})\\cdot \\frac{1}{5},\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}⟩ \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{5}),\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(s) & =‖{r}^{″}(s)‖ \\\\  & =|-\\frac{1}{5}|\\sqrt{{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{5}))}^{2}+{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{5}))}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})+{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-80523" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5e94acaae172a715aeef078197f31f678d672b149d01e9b726683c3b9ee790e8"} {"question" "q-80523" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-80523" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "5"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{25}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-80523" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{5}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-132559" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by its arc length $s$, where\n\n$$\nr(s)=⟨s-2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡s,\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡({s}^{2}+1)⟩,\\,s\\ge 0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-132559" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $T(s)$ denote the unit tangent to the given curve as a function of the arc length $s.$ Since we are given the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by the arc length $s$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(s)=‖{T}^{′}(s)‖=‖{r}^{″}(s)‖\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(s)$ and ${r}^{″}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(s-2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡s),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({s}^{2}+1))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{{s}^{2}-1}{{s}^{2}+1},\\,\\frac{2s}{{s}^{2}+1}⟩ \\\\ {r}^{″}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{{s}^{2}-1}{{s}^{2}+1}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{2s}{{s}^{2}+1})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{4s}{({s}^{2}+1)^{2}},\\,\\frac{2(1-{s}^{2})}{({s}^{2}+1)^{2}}⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{({s}^{2}+1)^{2}}⟨4s,\\,2(1-{s}^{2})⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(s) & =‖{r}^{″}(s)‖ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{({s}^{2}+1)^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{(4s)^{2}+{(2(1-{s}^{2}))}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{({s}^{2}+1)^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{16{s}^{2}+4{s}^{4}-8{s}^{2}+4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{({s}^{2}+1)^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{4{s}^{4}+8{s}^{2}+4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{({s}^{2}+1)^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{4({s}^{2}+1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2({s}^{2}+1)}{({s}^{2}+1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-132559" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5e94acaae172a715aeef078197f31f678d672b149d01e9b726683c3b9ee790e8"} {"question" "q-132559" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-132559" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{s}^{2}+1}}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}+1}"] ["math" "\\frac{s}{({s}^{2}+1)^{2}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-132559" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}+1}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-80545" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by its arc length $s,$ where\n\n$$\nr(s)=⟨\\frac{1}{3}(1-2s)^{3/2},\\,\\frac{1}{3}(2s)^{3/2}⟩,\\,0<s<\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-80545" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $T(s)$ denote the unit tangent to the given curve as a function of the arc length $s.$ Since we are given the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by the arc length $s$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(s)=‖{T}^{′}(s)‖=‖{r}^{″}(s)‖\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(s)$ and ${r}^{″}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{1}{3}(1-2s)^{3/2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{1}{3}(2s)^{3/2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}\\cdot (1-2s)^{1/2}\\cdot (-2),\\,\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}\\cdot (2s)^{1/2}\\cdot 2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-(1-2s)^{1/2},\\,(2s)^{1/2}⟩ \\\\ {r}^{″}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-(1-2s)^{1/2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}((2s)^{1/2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (1-2s)^{-1/2}\\cdot (-2),\\,\\frac{1}{2}(2s)^{-1/2}\\cdot 2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨(1-2s)^{-1/2},\\,(2s)^{-1/2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nFinally, the curvature is  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(s) & =‖{r}^{″}(s)‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{((1-2s)^{-1/2})}^{2}+{((2s)^{-1/2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(1-2s)^{-1}+(2s)^{-1}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{1-2s}+\\frac{1}{2s}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2s(1-2s)}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-80545" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5e94acaae172a715aeef078197f31f678d672b149d01e9b726683c3b9ee790e8"} {"question" "q-80545" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-80545" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-2s}}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2s(1-2s)}}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2s}}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2s(1-2s)}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-80545" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2s(1-2s)}}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-83665" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(t)$ given that its derivative ${r}^{′}(t)$ and the derivative of the corresponding unit tangent ${T}^{′}(t)$ are as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t)=⟨1,\\,t⟩,\\,{T}^{′}(t)=⟨-\\frac{t}{(1+{t}^{2})^{3/2}},\\,\\frac{1}{(1+{t}^{2})^{3/2}}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-83665" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since we are given both the derivative of the curve ${r}^{′}(t)$ and the derivative of the unit tangent ${T}^{′}(t)$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the magnitudes of ${r}^{′}(t)$ and ${T}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(-\\frac{t}{(1+{t}^{2})^{3/2}})}^{2}+{(\\frac{1}{(1+{t}^{2})^{3/2}})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{t}^{2}}{(1+{t}^{2})^{3}}+\\frac{1}{(1+{t}^{2})^{3}}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{(1+{t}^{2})^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(1+{t}^{2})} \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(1)^{2}+{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+{t}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(1+{t}^{2})}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{t}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(1+{t}^{2})^{3/2}}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-83665" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5e94acaae172a715aeef078197f31f678d672b149d01e9b726683c3b9ee790e8"} {"question" "q-83665" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-83665" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1+{t}^{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{(1+{t}^{2})^{3/2}}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{1+{t}^{2}}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{t}^{2}}}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{1+{t}^{2}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-83665" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{(1+{t}^{2})^{3/2}}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-64661" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(t)$ given that its derivative ${r}^{′}(t)$ and the derivative of the corresponding unit tangent ${T}^{′}(t)$ are as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t)=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,i+2\\,j-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,k,\\,{T}^{′}(t)=-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,i+\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-64661" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since we are given both the derivative of the curve ${r}^{′}(t)$ and the derivative of the unit tangent ${T}^{′}(t)$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the magnitudes of ${r}^{′}(t)$ and ${T}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)}^{2}+{(0)}^{2}+{(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2({cos}^{2}⁡2t+{sin}^{2}⁡2t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2} \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4({sin}^{2}⁡2t+{cos}^{2}⁡2t)+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4\\cdot 2} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the curvature is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2\\sqrt{2}}=\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-64661" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5e94acaae172a715aeef078197f31f678d672b149d01e9b726683c3b9ee790e8"} {"question" "q-64661" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-64661" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "4"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{8}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-64661" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-80614" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(t)$ given that its derivative ${r}^{′}(t)$ and the derivative of the corresponding unit tangent ${T}^{′}(t)$ are as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t)=\\,i-\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{4-{t}^{2}}}\\,j,\\,{T}^{′}(t)=-\\frac{t}{2\\sqrt{4-{t}^{2}}}\\,i-\\frac{1}{2}\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-80614" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since we are given both the derivative of the curve ${r}^{′}(t)$ and the derivative of the unit tangent ${T}^{′}(t)$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the magnitudes of ${r}^{′}(t)$ and ${T}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{(-\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{4-{t}^{2}}})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+\\frac{{t}^{2}}{4-{t}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{4-{t}^{2}+{t}^{2}}{4-{t}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{4-{t}^{2}}} \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(-\\frac{t}{2\\sqrt{4-{t}^{2}}})}^{2}+{(-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{t}^{2}}{4(4-{t}^{2})}+\\frac{1}{4}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{t}^{2}+4-{t}^{2}}{4(4-{t}^{2})}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4-{t}^{2}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}=\\frac{(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4-{t}^{2}}})}{(\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{4-{t}^{2}}})}=\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-80614" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5e94acaae172a715aeef078197f31f678d672b149d01e9b726683c3b9ee790e8"} {"question" "q-80614" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-80614" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-80614" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-64666" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(t)$ given that its derivative ${r}^{′}(t)$ and the derivative of the corresponding unit tangent ${T}^{′}(t)$ are as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\sqrt{3}\\,j+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,k,\\,{T}^{′}(t)=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}{2}\\,i-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{2}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-64666" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since we are given both the derivative of the curve ${r}^{′}(t)$ and the derivative of the unit tangent ${T}^{′}(t)$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the magnitudes of ${r}^{′}(t)$ and ${T}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}{2})}^{2}+{(0)}^{2}+{(\\frac{-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{4}({cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(\\sqrt{3})^{2}+(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)+3} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the curvature is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}=\\frac{(\\frac{1}{2})}{2}=\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-64666" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5e94acaae172a715aeef078197f31f678d672b149d01e9b726683c3b9ee790e8"} {"question" "q-64666" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-64666" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{8}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-64666" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{4}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-131230" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point $t>0$ on the curve $r(t)$ given that its derivative ${r}^{′}(t)$ and the derivative of the corresponding unit tangent ${T}^{′}(t)$ are as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t)=⟨2t,\\,-3{t}^{2}⟩,\\,{T}^{′}(t)=-\\frac{6}{(9{t}^{2}+4)^{3/2}}⟨3t,\\,2⟩,\\,t\\ge 0\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-131230" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since we are given both the derivative of the curve ${r}^{′}(t)$ and the derivative of the unit tangent ${T}^{′}(t)$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the magnitudes of ${r}^{′}(t)$ and ${T}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\frac{6}{(9{t}^{2}+4)^{3/2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{{(3t)}^{2}+{(2)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{(9{t}^{2}+4)^{3/2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{9{t}^{2}+4} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{9{t}^{2}+4} \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(2t)}^{2}+{(-3{t}^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+9{t}^{4}} \\\\  & =t\\sqrt{9{t}^{2}+4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{6}{9{t}^{2}+4})}{t\\sqrt{9{t}^{2}+4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{t(9{t}^{2}+4)^{3/2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-131230" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5e94acaae172a715aeef078197f31f678d672b149d01e9b726683c3b9ee790e8"} {"question" "q-131230" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-131230" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{9{t}^{2}+4}}"] ["math" "\\frac{3t}{(9{t}^{2}+4)^{3/2}}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{{t}^{2}\\sqrt{9{t}^{2}+4}}"] ["math" "\\frac{6t}{(9{t}^{2}+4)^{2}}"] ["math" "\\frac{6}{t(9{t}^{2}+4)^{3/2}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "q-131230" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{6}{t(9{t}^{2}+4)^{3/2}}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/state.json" "file_sha256" "4a471e488d507cf8782d4303394084d26f04900b5f027cce3e1b6b169ca586a0"} {"question" "e-3135" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the curve $\\mathbf r(s)$ parametrized by arc length $s.$ Find the curvature at the point where $s=\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}$ if the unit tangent vector of the curve is given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf T(s) = -\\dfrac{4}{5}\\sin{s}\\,\\mathbf i+\\dfrac{3}{5} \\sin{s}\\, \\mathbf j + \\cos{s}\\,\\mathbf k.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/example-3135.json" "file_sha256" "79185213cb938018ffb627a0649f23421689721f376782f240649009f311c1bc"} {"question" "e-3135" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since we are given that $\\mathbf{r}(s)$ and its unit tangent vector $\\mathbf T(s)$ are both parametrized by the arc length $s,$ we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\n\\kappa(s) = \\| \\mathbf T'(s) \\|\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $\\mathbf T(s)$ with respect to $s$ and evaluate it at $s=\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡s)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡s)j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡s)k \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡s\\,i+\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡s\\,j-\\operatorname{sin}⁡s\\,k \\\\ {T}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =-\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\,i+\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\,j-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\,k \\\\  & =0\\,i+0\\,j-k \\\\  & =-k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain the curvature at the point where $s=\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =‖{T}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})‖=‖-k‖=\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{0}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/example-3135.json" "file_sha256" "79185213cb938018ffb627a0649f23421689721f376782f240649009f311c1bc"} {"question" "e-3141" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $\\mathbf r(s)$ parametrized by its arc length $s$, where\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(s) = \\left\\langle \\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cos s , \\: -\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cos s, \\: \\sin s \\right\\rangle,\n\\quad 0\\leq s \\lt 2\\pi.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/example-3141.json" "file_sha256" "a8593dd90f986144e664dc9060f3a5d5c388a66001776eb8c387b2418c5d3582"} {"question" "e-3141" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $\\mathbf T(s)$ denote the unit tangent to the given curve as a function of the arc length $s.$ Since we are given the curve $\\mathbf{r}(s)$ parametrized by the arc length $s,$ we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\n\\kappa(s) = \\| \\mathbf T'(s) \\| = \\| \\mathbf{r}''(s) \\|\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate $\\mathbf r'(s)$ and $\\mathbf r''(s)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡s),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡s),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡s)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡s,\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡s,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡s⟩ \\\\ {r}^{″}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡s),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡s),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡s)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡s,\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡s,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡s⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the curvature is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(s) & =‖{r}^{″}(s)‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡s)}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡s)}^{2}+{(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡s)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{2}{cos}^{2}⁡s+\\frac{1}{2}{cos}^{2}⁡s+{sin}^{2}⁡s} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡s+{sin}^{2}⁡s} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/example-3141.json" "file_sha256" "a8593dd90f986144e664dc9060f3a5d5c388a66001776eb8c387b2418c5d3582"} {"question" "e-3140" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $\\mathbf r(t) = \\left\\langle 2\\sin t, \\:2\\cos t \\right\\rangle.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/example-3140.json" "file_sha256" "70c6e826902e93d91e1c792ad37f6081b64abace57b8dd089695c24418b1796f"} {"question" "e-3140" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $\\mathbf T(t)$ denote the unit tangent to the given curve as a function of the parameter $t.$ Since we are given the curve $\\mathbf{r}(t)$ parametrized by the parameter $t$ (not the arc length $s$), we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf \\kappa(t) = \\dfrac{\\left\\| \\mathbf T'(t) \\right\\|}{\\| \\mathbf r'(t) \\|}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate $\\mathbf r'(t)$ and find its magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}+(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4({cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the corresponding unit tangent vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}⟨2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate $\\mathbf T'(t)$ and find its magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩ \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}=\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068832/example-3140.json" "file_sha256" "70c6e826902e93d91e1c792ad37f6081b64abace57b8dd089695c24418b1796f"}] "usage" {"e-3135" [] "e-3140" [] "e-3141" []} "basis" 2319 "retractions" [[17592186119491 :question/problem "Consider the curve $\\mathbf r(s)$ parametrized by arc length $s$. Find the curvature at the point where $s=\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}$ if the unit tangent vector of the curve is given by\n$\\mathbf T(s) = -\\dfrac{4}{5}\\sin{s}\\,\\mathbf i+\\dfrac{3}{5} \\sin{s}\\, \\mathbf j + \\cos{s}\\,\\mathbf k$."] [17592186119491 :question/worked-solution "Since we are given that $\\mathbf{r}(s)$ and its unit tangent vector $\\mathbf T(s)$ are both parametrized by the arc length $s$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\n\\kappa(s) = \\| \\mathbf T'(s) \\|\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $\\mathbf T(s)$ with respect to $s$ and evaluate it at\n\n$$\ns=\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nT^{′}(s) &= \\frac{d}{ds}(-\\frac{4}{5}\\sin s)i + \\frac{d}{ds}(\\frac{3}{5}\\sin s)j + \\frac{d}{ds}(\\cos s)k \\\\\n&=-\\frac{4}{5}\\cos si + \\frac{3}{5}\\cos sj - \\sin sk \\\\\nT^{′}(\\frac{π}{2}) &= -\\frac{4}{5}\\cos (\\frac{π}{2})i + \\frac{3}{5}\\cos (\\frac{π}{2})j - \\sin (\\frac{π}{2})k \\\\\n&= 0i + 0j - k \\\\\n&=-k\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain the curvature at the point where\n\n$$\ns=\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nκ(\\frac{π}{2}) &= ‖T^{′}(\\frac{π}{2})‖ = ‖- k‖ = \\sqrt{0^{2} + 0^{2} + (-1)^{2}} = 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186119493 :question/problem "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $\\mathbf r(s)$ parametrized by its arc length $s$, where\n$\\mathbf r(s) = \\left\\langle \\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cos s, \\: -\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cos s, \\: \\sin s \\right\\rangle, \\quad 0\\leq s \\lt 2\\pi$."] [17592186119493 :question/worked-solution "Let $\\mathbf T(s)$ denote the unit tangent to the given curve as a function of the arc length $s$. Since we are given the curve $\\mathbf{r}(s)$ parametrized by the arc length $s$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\n\\kappa(s) = \\| \\mathbf T'(s) \\| = \\| \\mathbf{r}''(s) \\|\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate $\\mathbf r'(s)$ and $\\mathbf r''(s)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr^{′}(s) &= ⟨\\frac{d}{ds}(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cos s), \\frac{d}{ds}(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cos s), \\frac{d}{ds}(\\sin s)⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨ - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\sin s, \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\sin s, \\cos s⟩ \\\\\nr^{″}(s) &= ⟨\\frac{d}{ds}(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\sin s), \\frac{d}{ds}(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\sin s), \\frac{d}{ds}(\\cos s)⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨ - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cos s, \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cos s,-\\sin s⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nκ(s) &= ‖r^{″}(s)‖ \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cos s)^{2} + (\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cos s)^{2} + (-\\sin s)^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{2}\\cos^{2} s + \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^{2} s + \\sin^{2} s} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{\\cos^{2} s + \\sin^{2} s} \\\\\n&= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186119492 :question/problem "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $\\mathbf r(t) = \\left\\langle 2\\sin t, \\:2\\cos t \\right\\rangle$."] [17592186119492 :question/worked-solution "Let $\\mathbf T(t)$ denote the unit tangent to the given curve as a function of the parameter $t$. Since we are given the curve $\\mathbf{r}(t)$ parametrized by the parameter $t$ (not the arc length $s$), we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf \\kappa(t) = \\dfrac{\\left\\| \\mathbf T'(t) \\right\\|}{\\| \\mathbf r'(t) \\|}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate $\\mathbf r'(t)$ and find its magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr^{′}(t) &= ⟨\\frac{d}{dt}(2\\sin t), \\frac{d}{dt}(2\\cos t)⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨2\\cos t,-2\\sin t⟩ \\\\\n‖r^{′}(t)‖ &= \\sqrt{(2\\cos t)^{2} + (-2\\sin t)^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{4(\\cos^{2} t + \\sin^{2} t)} \\\\\n&= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the corresponding unit tangent vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nT(t) &= (r^{′}(t))/(‖r^{′}(t)‖) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}⟨2\\cos t,-2\\sin t⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨\\cos t,-\\sin t⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate $\\mathbf T'(t)$ and find its magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nT^{′}(t) &= ⟨\\frac{d}{dt}(\\cos t), \\frac{d}{dt}(-\\sin t)⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨ - \\sin t,-\\cos t⟩ \\\\\n‖T^{′}(t)‖ &= \\sqrt{(-\\sin t)^{2} + (-\\cos t)^{2}} \\\\\n&= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nκ(t) &= (‖T^{′}(t)‖)/(‖r^{′}(t)‖) = \\frac{1}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
